## Fix 1 (F1): internal/config TestDefaults reads the host config
`internal/config/config_test.go:22 TestDefaults` calls `Initialize()` from the package dir, so config discovery walks up into this repo's committed `.beads/config.yaml` (w28: `no-daemon: true`, `auto-start-daemon: false`) and the `no-daemon` and `auto-start-daemon` subtests fail. It is the same host-config leak the previous run fixed in `cmd/bd/autostart_test.go` with `isolateConfig(t)`. Apply the same isolation here: chdir into a temp dir holding an empty `.beads/config.yaml` (the empty project file is what stops the upward walk before the `~/.config/bd/config.yaml` fallback), call `Initialize()`, restore cwd and re-`Initialize()` on cleanup. The helper lives in package `main` under cmd/bd and cannot be imported; a small in-package copy in `internal/config` test code is fine. Do not touch the assertions or the repo config. Check whether any other test in `internal/config` needs the same treatment.

## Fix 2 (F2): upsertIssues lacks the multi-repo short-circuit
`internal/importer/importer.go` ~line 626: `handlePrefixMismatch` short-circuits membership entirely in multi-repo mode (`buildAllowedPrefixSet` returns nil when `config.GetMultiRepoConfig() != nil`), as the plan's Design says. The new `sameProject` test in `upsertIssues` does not, so in multi-repo mode a foreign-repo rename (db holds `other-1`, incoming same content as `other-2`, db prefix `bd`) now fails the configured-prefix test and is silently counted as Skipped, where before the item it took the `ExtractIssuePrefix` comparison path. Restore today's behaviour for that mode: when `config.GetMultiRepoConfig() != nil`, use the `ExtractIssuePrefix` comparison exactly as the empty-prefix branch does. Smallest change: fold the multi-repo test into the condition that already selects the guessing branch, with a comment naming GH#686. No new test unless one exists nearby you can extend in two lines.

